    On Windows, stop a dragged window bouncing between mixed-DPI monitors
    
    While the window is in a live move, apply the rect suggested by
    WM_DPICHANGED instead of the conservative rect. The conservative rect
    can land back on the monitor being left, which sends another
    WM_DPICHANGED and grows the window on every crossing.
    
    Same approach as rust-windowing/winit#4341 (merged) and #4694.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

